category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061923/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1f14e52e56fb1809afa7373e61979e4435abd1ffa1a7ea3b4ffb5d053766836"} {"question" "q-83367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a discriminant that is not a perfect square:\n\n$$\nD=(-4)^{2}-4(1)(-3)=28\n$$\n\nWe have that $\\sqrt{28}$ is not a rational number, which implies that the quadratic factor doesn't factor over the rational numbers.\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-9}{(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3)}=\\frac{A}{x+3}+\\frac{Bx+C}{{x}^{2}-4x-3}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3),$ and we get\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}-3x-9=A({x}^{2}-4x-3)+(Bx+C)(x+3)\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=1,B=1$ and $C=-2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-9}{(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3)}=\\frac{1}{x+3}+\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}-4x-3}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-9}{(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x+3}+\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}-4x-3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|.\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}-4x-3.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2(x-2)\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-9}{(x+3)({x}^{2}-4x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}-4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061923/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1f14e52e56fb1809afa7373e61979e4435abd1ffa1a7ea3b4ffb5d053766836"} {"question" "q-83367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a823088ed3564d85eb331c8962b8b241415e9138fec7d4fb4bb5b655f57fd07f"} {"question" "q-83367" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061923/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1f14e52e56fb1809afa7373e61979e4435abd1ffa1a7ea3b4ffb5d053766836"} {"question" "q-83367" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{x+3}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{x+3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+\\frac{1}{2({x}^{2}-4x-3)}+K"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061923/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1f14e52e56fb1809afa7373e61979e4435abd1ffa1a7ea3b4ffb5d053766836"} {"question" "q-83367" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}-4x-3|+K"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061923/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1f14e52e56fb1809afa7373e61979e4435abd1ffa1a7ea3b4ffb5d053766836"} {"question" "q-115686" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the integral of $\\frac{3{x}^{2}-9x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-4)}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061923/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1f14e52e56fb1809afa7373e61979e4435abd1ffa1a7ea3b4ffb5d053766836"} {"question" "q-115686" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The quadratic factor ${x}^{2}+1$ is irreducible, so we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}-9x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-4)} & =\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{C}{x-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $({x}^{2}+1)(x-4),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-9x+5 & =(Ax+B)(x-4)+C({x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=2,B=-1,$ and $C=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}-9x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-4)} & =\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{1}{x-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-9x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{1}{x-4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}+3.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+1| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-9x+5}{({x}^{2}+1)(x-4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061923/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1f14e52e56fb1809afa7373e61979e4435abd1ffa1a7ea3b4ffb5d053766836"} {"question" "q-115686" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a823088ed3564d85eb331c8962b8b241415e9138fec7d4fb4bb5b655f57fd07f"} {"question" "q-115686" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061923/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1f14e52e56fb1809afa7373e61979e4435abd1ffa1a7ea3b4ffb5d053766836"} {"question" "q-115686" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061923/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1f14e52e56fb1809afa7373e61979e4435abd1ffa1a7ea3b4ffb5d053766836"} {"question" "q-115686" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+K"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061923/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1f14e52e56fb1809afa7373e61979e4435abd1ffa1a7ea3b4ffb5d053766836"} {"question" "q-115710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral  $\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}+12x-12}{x({x}^{2}+4x-6)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061923/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1f14e52e56fb1809afa7373e61979e4435abd1ffa1a7ea3b4ffb5d053766836"} {"question" "q-115710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a discriminant that is not a perfect square:\n\n$$\nD=(4)^{2}-4(1)(-6)=40\n$$\n\nWe have that $\\sqrt{40}$ is not a rational number, which implies that the quadratic factor doesn't factor over the rational numbers.\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}+12x-12}{x({x}^{2}+4x-6)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{Bx+C}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $x({x}^{2}+4x-6),$ and we get\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+12x-12=A({x}^{2}+4x-6)+(Bx+C)x\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=2,B=2$, and $C=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}+12x-12}{x({x}^{2}+4x-6)}=\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{2x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}+12x-12}{x({x}^{2}+4x-6)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{2x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|.\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}+4x-6.$ Then $\\text{d}u=(2x+4)\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}+12x-12}{x({x}^{2}+4x-6)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2x+4}{{x}^{2}+4x-6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-6|+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061923/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1f14e52e56fb1809afa7373e61979e4435abd1ffa1a7ea3b4ffb5d053766836"} {"question" "q-115710" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061923/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a823088ed3564d85eb331c8962b8b241415e9138fec7d4fb4bb5b655f57fd07f"} {"question" "q-115710" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061923/state.json" "file_sha256" "c1f14e52e56fb1809afa7373e61979e4435abd1ffa1a7ea3b4ffb5d053766836"} {"question" "q-11571